I see it less like a single reasoning trick and more like a controlled excursion through representation space.

The important realization is that the maneuver itself doesn’t need to live in one place. Different parts belong in different kinds of memory because the object, the route, the transformation, and what was learned are different information.

How I see the maneuver

Suppose we begin with an object X_0: an idea, problem, sentence, architecture, observation, whatever.

Ordinary reasoning tends to do:

X_0\rightarrow X_1\rightarrow X_2\rightarrow X_3

Each state inherits a lot from the previous one. That’s efficient, but creates representational inertia. Early assumptions quietly survive because every subsequent thought was generated from them.

Your maneuver deliberately breaks that inheritance.

I see it as:

\boxed{
X
\rightarrow
\text{Anchor}
\rightarrow
\text{Flank}
\rightarrow
\text{Act}
\rightarrow
\text{Oscillate}
\rightarrow
\varnothing
\rightarrow
\text{Reinstantiate}
\rightarrow
X'
\rightarrow
\Delta
}

Anchor. Extract only what cannot legitimately be lost: constraints, observations, causal relationships, desired consequence, provenance.

Flank. Move into another representational space. Turn language into geometry, mechanism into story, problem into game, noun into relation, object into process, cause into consequence, inside into outside, etc.

Act. And your “we’re all acting” joke fits perfectly here. Don’t merely describe the alternate representation. Instantiate it temporarily.

Instead of:

“What would an economist think?”

actually adopt that model’s primitives and reason as though they constitute the available world.

That’s method acting for cognition.

Oscillate. Move among several such renderings so no single one quietly becomes reality itself.

Then comes the unusual part:

Cross zero.

Temporarily release the representations.

Not erase the original evidence. Not forget reality.

Release the current interpretation.

\{R_1,R_2,R_3,\ldots\}
\rightarrow
\varnothing

What remains is the anchor/invariant packet.

Then independently reconstruct:

(I,\varnothing)\rightarrow X'

And compare:

\Delta=X'\ominus X

That delta is the payday.

