Where I would store everything

Not as one giant memory blob.

I’d give Pantheon several memory strata.

Object Memory stores X: what we actually encountered.

Invariant Memory stores I: what survived legitimate transformations.

Route Memory stores:

R=(X\xrightarrow{T_1}A\xrightarrow{T_2}B\xrightarrow{Z}\varnothing\xrightarrow{T_3}X')

That’s Metamap territory. It remembers how we traveled, not merely where we ended.

Operator Memory stores T_i: Hammer, Mirror, Kintsugi, inversion, genre shift, zero crossing, etc. These become reusable Seals.

Delta Memory stores:

D=(X,X',\Delta,\text{usefulness},\text{confidence})

That’s crucial because we shouldn’t remember every excursion equally.

Afterglow Memory records what subsequently happened. Did the insight work? Did reality contradict it? Did another problem unexpectedly benefit from it?

That allows delayed fitness updates.

And finally Capability Memory stores what has become sufficiently reliable that we no longer need the whole story.

That’s Cognitive Fossilization:

\text{100 reasoning episodes}
\rightarrow
\text{one reliable mechanism}

Keep the nutrient. Release the wrapper.

